  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25229178",
      "title": "Deploying NextJS Projects",
      "lectureOrder": 447,
      "videoOrder": 414,
      "sourceHash": "62cf1489946c2282f73941857a71b63b1dc7ba3b6000df7e70de399efca5e437",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 5.09,
          "en": "Now, when it comes to deploying NextJS apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.09,
          "end": 7.98,
          "en": "there are different hosting providers you can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.98,
          "end": 9.42,
          "en": "and there are different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.42,
          "end": 11.91,
          "en": "of configuring your project as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.91,
          "end": 14.94,
          "en": "You can, for example, use environment variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.94,
          "end": 19.75,
          "en": "For example, to hold things like your database credentials.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.75,
          "end": 21.94,
          "en": "I'll not dive into that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.94,
          "end": 25.12,
          "en": "I do in my full next JS course, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.12,
          "end": 27.7,
          "en": "But for this example here we'll just keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.7,
          "end": 30.54,
          "en": "the credentials stored here in this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.54,
          "end": 34.33,
          "en": "and from a security perspective, this is fine by the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.33,
          "end": 37.91,
          "en": "because this code will never end up on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.91,
          "end": 39.88,
          "en": "It just might be unconvenient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.88,
          "end": 43.93,
          "en": "to use one and the same database and one and the same user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.93,
          "end": 46.21,
          "en": "for development and for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.21,
          "end": 48.21,
          "en": "But for this demo, this does not matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.21,
          "end": 50.62,
          "en": "So I'll stick to this approach here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.62,
          "end": 52.63,
          "en": "And regarding the hosting provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.63,
          "end": 54.545,
          "en": "I will use Vercel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.545,
          "end": 58.7,
          "en": "Vercel is a great hosting provider for NextJS applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.7,
          "end": 62.16,
          "en": "because the Vercel actually is a hosting provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.16,
          "end": 65.67,
          "en": "by the same team that's developed NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.67,
          "end": 68.44,
          "en": "So it's really embracing NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.44,
          "end": 72.99,
          "en": "and optimized for NextJS if you wanna put it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.99,
          "end": 76.33,
          "en": "And deploying NextJS applications to Vercel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.33,
          "end": 79.393,
          "en": "is thankfully also extremely simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.48,
          "end": 83.9,
          "en": "Now what you'll need to do to start deploying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.9,
          "end": 88.3,
          "en": "is sign up with a Git repository provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.3,
          "end": 91.55,
          "en": "because with Vercel you will directly link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.55,
          "end": 93.7,
          "en": "your GitHub repository,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.7,
          "end": 96.47999999999999,
          "en": "which holds your source code, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.47999999999999,
          "end": 100.24000000000001,
          "en": "to Vercel and they will then get your source code from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.24000000000001,
          "end": 102.963,
          "en": "that repository and deploy it for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.82,
          "end": 107.46000000000001,
          "en": "Therefore you need to use GitHub, GitLab, or Bitbucket,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.46000000000001,
          "end": 110.28999999999999,
          "en": "which are Git repository providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.28999999999999,
          "end": 114.88,
          "en": "to put your code there before you can deploy it with Vercel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.88,
          "end": 118.2,
          "en": "Now here I will use GitHub, which arguably is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.2,
          "end": 121.63,
          "en": "the biggest and most popular Git repository provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.63,
          "end": 124.57300000000001,
          "en": "And I already did log in with my account here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.52,
          "end": 127.96,
          "en": "Once you did create an account and login,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.96,
          "end": 128.88,
          "en": "it's free,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.88,
          "end": 131.77,
          "en": "you can create a new repository",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.77,
          "end": 134.52,
          "en": "and you can give this repository any name you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.52,
          "end": 138.95,
          "en": "like NextJS course demo or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.95,
          "end": 140.69,
          "en": "You can also give it a description.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.69,
          "end": 144.06,
          "en": "And then chose whether it should be public or private.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.06,
          "end": 146.32,
          "en": "If it's public, everyone can see it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.32,
          "end": 147.82999999999998,
          "en": "Everyone can see your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.82999999999998,
          "end": 152.32,
          "en": "If it's private only people you grant access to can view it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.32,
          "end": 154.3,
          "en": "And I'll go with private here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.3,
          "end": 156.62,
          "en": "but either of the options can be correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.62,
          "end": 160.13,
          "en": "It simply depends on which kind of project it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.13,
          "end": 163.323,
          "en": "If it's a open source project it will probably be public.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.3,
          "end": 167.543,
          "en": "So I'll go with private and create my repository.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.49,
          "end": 172.05,
          "en": "Once that is created, you need to push your code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.05,
          "end": 175.87,
          "en": "Now for that you need to install Git on your local system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.87,
          "end": 179.81,
          "en": "and you can git git-scm.com.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.81,
          "end": 182.22,
          "en": "It's available for all operating systems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.22,
          "end": 184.23,
          "en": "You can download the installer from there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.23,
          "end": 187.863,
          "en": "and simply walk through it to install Git on your system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.85,
          "end": 191.85,
          "en": "And once you installed get on your local system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.85,
          "end": 195.62,
          "en": "you can create a so-called commit in your project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.62,
          "end": 197.6,
          "en": "a code snapshot, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.6,
          "end": 199.45,
          "en": "And then push that commit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.45,
          "end": 203.13,
          "en": "that repository as a whole, actually, to GitHub",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 203.13,
          "end": 207,
          "en": "to move your code with your code history to GitHub.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207,
          "end": 210.04,
          "en": "Now, I won't turn this course into a Git course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.04,
          "end": 212.4,
          "en": "If you wanna learn more about Git and GitHub",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.4,
          "end": 215.23,
          "en": "we got a standalone course on that which you can take.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.23,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "Here I will assume that you have those Git basics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 220.42000000000002,
          "en": "and that you have Git installed now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 220.42000000000002,
          "end": 222.03,
          "en": "And if you have it installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.03,
          "end": 224.97,
          "en": "you can then go back into your local project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 224.97,
          "end": 229.03,
          "en": "into your project folder and create a code snapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.03,
          "end": 231.1,
          "en": "a commit as it's called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.1,
          "end": 234.23,
          "en": "You do this by running git add dot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 234.23,
          "end": 236.92000000000002,
          "en": "and you can run this if you got Git installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.92000000000002,
          "end": 240.16,
          "en": "and then git commit and then some message of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 240.16,
          "end": 243.09,
          "en": "For example, ready for deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.09,
          "end": 246,
          "en": "Though typically you want to add commit messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 246,
          "end": 248.233,
          "en": "that describe what you changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.47,
          "end": 253.92,
          "en": "But with that, I now created such a snapshot, such a commit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 253.92,
          "end": 255.97,
          "en": "and now we're ready for deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.97,
          "end": 259.8,
          "en": "Now that means that now we need to push our code to GitHub.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.8,
          "end": 262.26,
          "en": "For this we can grab this URL here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.26,
          "end": 265.37,
          "en": "which will point to the repository we created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 265.37,
          "end": 270.37,
          "en": "And in our local project folder run git remote add origin",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 270.67,
          "end": 273.123,
          "en": "and paste that URL in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 274.25,
          "end": 276.55,
          "en": "Now depending on whether you worked with Git",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 276.55,
          "end": 278.31,
          "en": "and GitHub before or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.31,
          "end": 281.65,
          "en": "you might wanna add your GitHub username here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 281.65,
          "end": 284.31,
          "en": "in front of github.com.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 284.31,
          "end": 286.23,
          "en": "If you did work with GitHub before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.23,
          "end": 289.46,
          "en": "and push before you probably don't need to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 289.46,
          "end": 291.84000000000003,
          "en": "but if you never pushed anything to GitHub",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.84000000000003,
          "end": 293.29,
          "en": "adding this will ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 293.29,
          "end": 295.54,
          "en": "that you're prompted for your password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 295.54,
          "end": 298.83,
          "en": "and that you have a chance of entering your credentials,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.83,
          "end": 301.74,
          "en": "because of course you'll need to authenticate yourselves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 301.74,
          "end": 304.98,
          "en": "in order to successfully push to this repository.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.98,
          "end": 308.77,
          "en": "You can't just start pushing to some random repositories,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 308.77,
          "end": 310.4,
          "en": "which you don't own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.4,
          "end": 314.75,
          "en": "So therefore here I will now add this origin here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 314.75,
          "end": 318.67,
          "en": "and then run git push -- all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 318.67,
          "end": 321.41,
          "en": "And this will now push our code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 321.41,
          "end": 324.15,
          "en": "Now you might be prompted for your password here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 324.15,
          "end": 326.65,
          "en": "and you can then enter your GitHub password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 326.65,
          "end": 328.87,
          "en": "or you as a token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 328.87,
          "end": 330.12,
          "en": "for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 330.12,
          "end": 331.84,
          "en": "authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 331.84,
          "end": 333.81,
          "en": "For this to generate such a token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 333.81,
          "end": 336.73,
          "en": "you need to go to your GitHub settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 336.73,
          "end": 340.56,
          "en": "and then there go to developer settings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 340.56,
          "end": 342.483,
          "en": "personal access tokens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 343.43,
          "end": 346.27,
          "en": "and generate a new token here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 346.27,
          "end": 348.23,
          "en": "Once you confirm this with your password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 348.23,
          "end": 352.18,
          "en": "you can add some note here like NextJS deployment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 352.18,
          "end": 354.37,
          "en": "or a more general purpose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 354.37,
          "end": 357.323,
          "en": "And then under scopes select repo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 358.3,
          "end": 359.57,
          "en": "delete repo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 359.57,
          "end": 361.02,
          "en": "and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 361.02,
          "end": 363.023,
          "en": "admin repo hook here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 364.41,
          "end": 365.933,
          "en": "and then generate a token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 366.82,
          "end": 369.28,
          "en": "And now you'll need to copy that token here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 369.28,
          "end": 370.833,
          "en": "which is showing up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 371.98,
          "end": 375.67,
          "en": "and enter this as a password when you're prompted for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 375.67,
          "end": 378.82,
          "en": "Once you did all of that and you pushed successfully",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 378.82,
          "end": 381.73,
          "en": "you should see your code in this repository,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 381.73,
          "end": 384.883,
          "en": "which you just created in the main branch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 385.77,
          "end": 388.36,
          "en": "And now we can link this repository",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 388.36,
          "end": 391.09,
          "en": "to Vercel to start deploying.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 391.09,
          "end": 392.37,
          "en": "Now, before we do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 392.37,
          "end": 394.83,
          "en": "let me talk about building for production",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 394.83,
          "end": 397.4,
          "en": "and what Vercel actually does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 397.4,
